From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:33:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 166/202] [ae-patch] Deliver the lead's notice on plain-text
 native turns, tell child sessions they are helpers, and switch the model when
 a preset fixes the lead

The executor adapter flattened every text-only message to a string and dropped
the framework notice block, so plain-text native turns never received the team
and roles notice. The notice now rides along as a block next to one input_text
block, for the current turn only and only for the Claude and Codex native
executors, which read it; every other executor gets the plain string as before,
replayed history loses old notices, and steering still sends plain text. Child
sessions get one helper line instead of the lead's Auto or Team text (a fork
stays a lead). The lead line names the session's own model and effort and the
preset's model when it differs; only a Claude lead hears about the Agent tool
and tier aliases; an older model version keeps its full id. The roles block
drops "past that, ask first" when model changes are off. Picking a preset whose
lead is fixed (pill, Alt digit, a new pick in the dialog, START ON) also sets
the session's model and effort, resolved against the session's own harness and
checked against the session's own row, with a toast and Undo. Settings uses
"Own subagents only" for the Helpers rule everywhere and tags the model change
rules "Coming later".
